.TH KILL 1 "5th of August 2026" zenithutils "User Commands"

.SH NAME
kill - terminate one or multiple processes

.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
On Unix:
    \fBkill\fP \fI[-signal] pid|name [pid2|name2] ...\fP

On Windows:
    \fBkill\fP \fIpid|name [pid2|name2] ...\fP
.EE

.SH DESCRIPTION
Takes one or multiple pids or process names and terminates them
On Unix, a signal can be specified with the following syntaxes:
.EX
    kill -SIGKILL
    kill -KILL
    kill -9
.EE

.SH OPTIONS (unix only)
.TP
\fB-SIGNAL\fP
signal used to terminate the process, can be provided numerically, or via the name of the signal, or via the name of the signal prepended with "SIG"

.SH SEE ALSO
kill(2)
